{
  "_doc": "CINEMATIC STYLING -- how each troop reads as an anthropomorphized machine. Each archetype (from the class taglines + film canon) is reasoned into concrete numbers the game can apply on top of the base IQM parts + chassis, so a Reaver prowls hunched and predatory while a Prime stands noble and upright without needing separate meshes. Fields: posture_lean (deg forward, aggression/predation lean in), shoulder_hunch (0..0.2, predatory rounding), gait_cadence (step speed x, fast<->ponderous), gait_swagger (side sway x, heavy bots roll), arm_len/leg_len (proportion x flavor on top of chassis), visor_narrow (0 open/friendly .. 1 slit/menacing), visor_angle (brow tilt deg; negative = angry down-brow), idle_restless (0 calm .. 1 twitchy), aggression (0..1 behavioural bias). All are multipliers/offsets, safe to clamp.",
